<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Part of my concern here is that while I could see someone <em>deliberately</em> making a computer using strings and vibrations and the placement of rocks etc., I find it hard to believe that a largely unguided process like this would lead to the creation of an actually functional AI. Like there's a tipping point where it gets smart enough it could maybe manipulate stuff to further it's development, but before that, I'm not sure if it can? I think if presented well, this might not be an issue? Like particularly if you don't dwell on the origins.</p>
<p>Beyond this, my largest issue with this pitch is it's very focussed on 'how did the threadmaker get here' but to me the most interesting question is 'what does the existence of the threadmaker imply'.</p>
<p>Like, your central narrative section says:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Researchers try to figure out how Threadmother thinks and communicates, what her influence on mankind has been, and how she can be contained, if she even can be contained.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And I'm left wondering how you're going to get a reader invested in this, y'know? It feels to me that this might be lacking in stakes, but also like it might be too reliant on an info-dump about this SCP being interesting and I'm not sure it would be. But the idea of her having had influence on mankind and in turn, the foundation figuring out the extent of it and stuff sounds like it could be a great setting for a like, tense thriller; but for that to work, you need to like&#8230;actually do stuff?</p>
<p>You mention this is a thought experiment as to what the crudest construction of a computer could be: what if this article plays with that? With like, the bulk of the story being the Foundation trying to figure out if it's actually intelligent or not? The issue with this is you would need to settle on a definitive answer and it might feel hard to make it feel meaningful?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

