			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835829">
									

<p>Yeah, Spinner wasn't an optimal suggestion, also makes too many allusions to something spider-like, which isn't quite the case. I really liked Threadmother because it gives a bit of a warmer feel to the entity, it doesn't seem ominous or threatening. Other ideas I had was &quot;Auditor&quot; (someone who listens), &quot;The Braided Idol&quot;, &quot;Harmony&quot; and &quot;Sonority of Concord&quot;.</p>
<p>About the Sumerian link, I honestly thought that I would invent that part, and for the later parts I have historical images to use.</p>
<p>I've also got a good friend who's an illustrator who's making an image to use, so I'll use his as the main image, and then some images from greek/roman/norse mythology.</p>
<p>Francesca is a researcher yes, but the reason that it's done through interviews is because her logs haven't allowed the Foundation to do what she's done with the SCP. The Foundation is trying to figure out if she's deliberately withholding something from them, or what the reason is that they can't reproduce her results.</p>
<p>I have a very specific end in mind. My idea is that Francesca got her interest in musical theory in her childhood, hiding in her room she would put on music when things got too bad to drown out the sounds around her. The many hours she spent with the music developed her interest, which later became her profession.</p>
<p>In the end, an administrator and a number of researchers visit the site, having a heated discussion in glass room next to Threadmother about what to do with the SCP. Some are arguing for the destruction of the SCP. Francesca hears their heated argument, goes over to a stereo in the cave and puts on music to shield Threadmother from the argument, just as she used music to shield herself from her parents arguing. And that's the end.</p>
<p>(sidenote, they actually end up not destroying the SCP, but decide to have a smaller team run the site with Francesca as leader).</p>

